Ported components and their sources — campaign R1 (2026-08-30)

The R1 ops kit and serving-config bundle in this repository were derived from
the Reederey87 production kit — a downstream production fork of this recipe
running the same container image digest
(ghcr.io/miaai-lab/glm-5.3-flash-2x-dgx-sparks@sha256:9bb1557a4234fce63d59599e44d10747eabd742beb337eebf9e7070be8a0fd58),
byte-identical overlays, and the same benchmark protocol. Its measured results
(70.4 tok/s structured / 29.5 tok/s prose / ~893 tok/s prefill) are therefore
configuration-level findings, ported here and re-gated by our own benches.

Ported / derived in this campaign (all adapted to this kit's layout, ports and
.env names; upstream file names in parentheses):

  local/cache-burst.py            (cache-burst.py)   multi-session prefix-cache protocol
  local/cache-probe.sh            (cache-probe.sh)   gate wrapper
  tests/bench_prefix_cache.py     (bench_prefix_cache.py) AB-PLAN harness
  local/acceptance.sh             (acceptance.sh)    7-probe quality battery
  local/serving-probe.sh          (serving 6-probe)  liveness battery
  local/toolcall-probe.py         (toolcall-probe.py) tool-call acceptance battery
  local/xid-check.sh              (Xid monitor + timer)
  local/metrics-alert.sh          (metrics-alert + timer) spec-decode acceptance alerting
  local/check-updates.sh          (check-updates)    registry digest vs pin + 590.x driver warning
  local/prod-start.sh             (prod-start.sh)    memory-gated restart + config-shape JIT wipe
  fleet_watchdog.sh upgrades      (watchdog)         crash vs wedge vs deliberate-stop distinction
  start.sh bundle knobs           (serving config)   MNBT 3584, long-prefill threshold 1792,
                                                     VLLM_PREFIX_CACHE_RETENTION_INTERVAL=0,
                                                     --no-async-scheduling, KV pin procedure,
                                                     FLASHINFER_WORKSPACE_BASE persistence

Not adopted from upstream (recorded deviations):
  - Loopback bind (0.0.0.0 -> 127.0.0.1): REJECTED by operator — this kit keeps
    the LAN bind; the unauthenticated-LAN exposure is documented in README.
  - "MNBT < 3584 -> ~0% cache hits": contradicted by our measured 93% solo hits
    at MNBT=1024 (D1 evidence); retention env, not MNBT alone, is treated as the
    multi-session lever. MNBT=3584 adopted for the prefill benefit and re-gated
    by our own cache probes.

Upstream kit: Reederey87 (production fork of
MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks). Their measurements and operational
procedures are referenced throughout docs/CAMPAIGN-R1.md.
